{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBxvfUFqWkL1BPzMwVV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A `save_fact` no longer evicts the static instructions from the prompt cache. I haven't run it against the API, so the real effect on `logs/usage.jsonl` is still unconfirmed.\n\n**Cause:** `build_system()` put the coaching instructions and the per-athlete context, which includes the facts and today's date, into one system block with the `cache_control` marker. Any change to the facts changed the cached text, so the next call wrote the whole prompt to the cache again.\n\n**Change in `bot.py`:** the system prompt is now two blocks.\n- The instructions have the `cache_control` marker. They're identical for every athlete and every day, so they stay cached.\n- The athlete context (facts, zones, goal, date) follows with no marker. Changes to it no longer touch the cached prefix.\n\nI also updated the caching paragraph in `README.md` to match, and wrote `ANSWER.md` with the cause, the change and the open checks.\n\n**Verified without calling the API:** the instructions block is byte-identical before and after appending a fact and across a day change. It's shared between athletes, and only that block carries `cache_control`.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- **Minimum cacheable size.** The cached prefix is now tools plus instructions, which is close to Sonnet's 1024-token minimum. If it falls under, nothing gets cached and the change does nothing. After deploying, check that `cache_read_input_tokens` is non-zero on the calls after a `save_fact`.\n- **Keyword tool filtering still breaks the cache.** `select_tools()` changes the tools array, and tools come first in the cache prefix. I left it alone because NOTES.md records that filtering as a clear win. If the bill is still high, that's the next place to look.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"us